working at this hospital, contributing to its operations and patient care.", "VIRGINIA PEÑA CORTÉS:Virginia Peña Cortés is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital Virgen de la Salud in Toledo.", "NOELIA PELÁEZ TORRES:Noelia Peláez Torres is a medical professional in the endocrinology and nutrition section at Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias.", "PANCREATITIS CRÓNICA:Chronic pancreatitis, known as \"pancreatitis crónica,\" is a long-term inflammatory condition of the pancreas that results in irreversible structural changes. This chronic inflammation can lead to permanent damage, affecting both the exocrine and endocrine functions of the pancreas. As a consequence, individuals with chronic pancreatitis may experience various digestive issues and impaired insulin production, necessitating nutritional support and careful management of their condition.", "GLÁNDULA PANCREÁTICA:The pancreatic gland is responsible for the secretion of digestive enzymes and hormones such as insulin and glucagon, playing a crucial role in metabolism regulation.", "ISLOTES DE LANGERHANS:The islets of Langerhans are clusters of cells in the pancreas that produce insulin and glucagon, essential for carbohydrate metabolism regulation.", "CÁLCULOS BILIARES:Gallstones are solid particles that form in the gallbladder and are a leading cause of acute pancreatitis.", "TUMOR DE PAPILA DUODENAL:Duodenal papilla tumors are another condition that must be considered when diagnosing pancreatitis without a clear cause.", "DR. JOHN RANSON:Dr. John Ranson established criteria in 1974 to evaluate the severity and prognosis of pancreatitis, identifying patients at high risk of complications."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}